# Normalize line endings across platforms.
#
# Without this file, Windows checkouts (including GitHub Actions
# windows-latest runners) convert LF to CRLF via core.autocrlf=true,
# which makes prettier fail on every file because prettier's default
# `endOfLine: 'lf'` rejects CRLF. A CI run on Windows surfaced this —
# every .ts file got flagged.
#
# Pinning LF on the text formats we own keeps the working tree
# byte-identical across macOS / Linux / Windows contributors and
# CI runners.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Sources and configs — explicit LF.
*.ts text eol=lf
*.js text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.cjs text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.jsonc text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf
*.css text eol=lf

# Windows-only formats keep CRLF (don't break tooling that expects it).
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Binary — never touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.psd binary
*.icns binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.tgz binary
*.zip binary
